{
	"_note": "Adventures: everything pets are sent out to do. TYPES just group places (and what they're like); 'gear': false means trips there pack no gear, 'scout': false that they never take scout notes (data/errands.json). LOCATIONS form a branching map: only the one with 'start' is open at first; the rest open when a pet spots them on a trip ('leads_to': { to, spot = chance per trip that comes home }) or when a rumour leads there. 'map' places it on the pet's doodle map (x/y in map units, garden at 0,0; 'doodle' picks the drawing; 'note' is the pet's scribble); 'more': true draws a ? cloud beyond it. 'page' is which map page it's on (data/unlocks.json 'pages'); a place with 'start' is open as soon as its page is. A place has a fixed 'events' list, or a weighted 'pool' that each trip draws 'draws' events from without repeats; 'go_home': true adds a 'go home' option (keep the bag) to every event; 'part_slots' makes parts found there lean to those slots. 'minutes' is the whole trip, 'max_party' caps party size there, 'safe': true means nobody gets hurt or lost there (a failure just brings nothing: the garden, to learn how adventures go), 'difficulty' multiplies option difficulty, 'danger' how many get hurt or lost, 'loot' multiplies coins, 'box' is the box found there and the odds for part rarity; 'finish_rewards' is a treat bag for trips that go all the way (not home early). Rewards grow the further into a trip an event is (x1, x1.25, x1.5, ...). EVENTS are shared. Option: 'chance' is its own chance of going well (tilted a little by 'stat' and down if hurt); older options test 'stat' against 'difficulty'; no chance and no stat = always works; 'tag' is for policies; 'min_party' hides it for smaller parties. Outcome: 'lost'/'injured'/'heal' are [min, max] fractions of the party, 'hurt' is a fraction of pets that lose a heart ('hearts': 2 = both at once; a pet hurt twice doesn't come back, and nothing it found comes home), 'progress' is continue / end / skip, 'leave_injured' leaves the injured behind, 'rewards' is a list of { kind, ... } handled in scripts/adventure/rewards.gd (coins: 'amount' per pet; box/part/rumour/anything else: 'chance', growing with the square root of the party). RUMOURS are what exploring brings back: 'about' is how the pet describes it, 'unlocks' what saying yes opens, 'requires' what must be open before anyone can hear it. An event with 'find' gives a special item once (see data/unlocks.json): it stops turning up after it's been found; finds are 'auto': true (no question: the party does the first option by itself and walks on; a failed try just means it turns up again on a later trip); an event's 'min_party' skips it for smaller parties; '{i}' is 'i' for one pet, 'we' for a party; 'after' (a find id) keeps it away until that find is home; 'after_machine' (a node id on data/machine_tree.json) keeps it away until that node is fixed (the basket waits for the flap, so errands open once bits start holding the machine up). {who} is the pet's name, or 'the party'. Texts stay cheerful and plain.",
